 * `border-color` on every element. A rule that sets `border` / `border-color`
 * must reach (0,4,0): the two root classes (0,2,0) + the `data-part` REPEATED on
 * the target (0,2,0). Rules that set only non-border paint (background, color,
 * box-shadow, outline, transform) beat preflight while unlayered at (0,3,0). The
 * 4th unit is bought by REPEATING the `data-part`, never by an incidental
 * attribute a refactor could move (`role`, `aria-label`, `placeholder`). Pure
 * `border: none` resets carry no color and are exempt from the (0,4,0) floor.
 *
 * Values are transcribed verbatim from `engines/modern.tsx`.
