/**
 * Modern DetailPanel skin (WO-ARC-09 checkpoint 5).
 *
 * DELIBERATELY UNLAYERED, same rationale as the other engine skins (P-47):
 * every `rottay-*` layer sorts before Tailwind's `base` layer, so a layered
 * rule loses to preflight regardless of specificity. Unlayered outranks
 * preflight + DaisyUI and still yields to a caller's inline `style`.
 *
 * SCOPE ROOT is the panel's outer `<div>`, which carries the pair
 * `ds-pattern-detail-panel ds-engine-modern` + `data-part='root'`; every painted
 * element is a descendant with its own `data-part`. The engine has two roots —
 * the content panel and the loading early-return — and both carry the class pair,
 * `data-part='root'`, and (loading only) `data-loading='true'`.
 *
 * SPECIFICITY (P-48): the Platform-only Rottay artifact ships an unlayered
 * `html[data-tenant]:not([data-theme]):not(.light) *` at (0,3,1) that sets
 * `border-color` on every element. A rule that paints `border` / `border-color`
 * must reach (0,4,0): the two root classes (0,2,0) + a `data-part` REPEATED on
 * the target, or a contract `data-variant`/`data-active`/`data-disabled`, for the
 * remaining (0,2,0). Rules that set only non-border paint (background, color,
 * box-shadow, outline, border-radius) beat preflight while unlayered at (0,3,0).
 * The 4th unit is never bought from an incidental attribute (`role`, `aria-label`,
 * `placeholder`). Pure `border: none` resets carry no color and are exempt.
 *
 * Interaction paint that the removed React hover/focus state used to own now
 * lives here as `:hover, :focus` rules, gated on `:not(:disabled)` because the
 * button element is natively `disabled` whenever the action is disabled OR
 * loading — the exact `isInteractive` gate the JSX evaluated.
 *
 * Values are transcribed verbatim from `engines/modern.tsx`.
