/**
 * Rustic (Vanilla / CSS-variable) DetailPanel skin (WO-ARC-09 checkpoint 5).
 *
 * DELIBERATELY UNLAYERED (P-47), same rationale as the modern skin: a layered
 * rule loses to Tailwind preflight on layer order whatever its specificity;
 * unlayered outranks preflight + DaisyUI and still yields to a caller's inline
 * `style`.
 *
 * SCOPE ROOT is the panel's outer `<div>`, carrying the pair
 * `ds-pattern-detail-panel ds-engine-rustic` + `data-part='root'`; every painted
 * element is a descendant with a `data-part`.
 *
 * SPECIFICITY (P-48): the tenant `*` border-color floor sits at (0,3,1), so a
 * rule that paints `border` / `border-color` must reach (0,4,0) — the two root
 * classes (0,2,0) + a REPEATED `data-part`, or a contract
 * `data-variant`/`data-active`/`data-disabled` — never an incidental attribute
 * (`role`, `aria-label`, `placeholder`). Non-border paint beats preflight while
 * unlayered at (0,3,0). Pure `border: none` resets carry no color and are exempt;
 * a `border: 1px solid transparent` does NOT reset — its transparent color would
 * lose to the tenant floor below (0,4,0), so it repeats the data-part like any
 * other painting border.
 *
 * Interaction paint that the removed imperative `.style.*` handlers used to own
 * now lives here: the ghost/default hover tint as two `data-variant`-guarded
 * `:hover:not(:disabled)` rules (primary/danger explicitly excluded, as the JSX
 * guard was), and the double-ring focus indicator as one unconditional `:focus`
 * rule (all variants, as `onFocus` was). The old mouse-leave reset for the
 * `default` variant cleared its inline base to an empty string (a restore bug);
 * the CSS base rule restores the true factory base after hover instead — a
 * structural fix, not a reproduced bug.
 *
 * Values are transcribed verbatim from `engines/rustic.tsx`.
 */

/* ---- pulse keyframes: rustic's skeleton dims to opacity .4 (dimmer than the
        global keyframes.css `pulse`, which bottoms at .5). Renamed off `pulse`
        so this globally-loaded definition does not redefine the shared one; the
        skeleton's inline `animation` references this name. ---- */
@keyframes ds-detail-panel-pulse {
  0%, 100% { opacity: 1; }
  50% { opacity: 0.4; }
}

/* ---- root: container surface, border, radius, inherited text color, shadow ---- */
.ds-pattern-detail-panel.ds-engine-rustic[data-part='root'][data-part='root'] {
  color: var(--ds-color-neutral-900);
  background: var(--ds-color-neutral-0, #fff);
