/**
 * Modern DataTable skin (WO-ARC-09 checkpoint 6).
 *
 * DELIBERATELY UNLAYERED, same rationale the other engine skins state in full
 * (P-47): every `rottay-*` cascade layer sorts before Tailwind's `base` layer,
 * so a layered rule loses to preflight regardless of specificity. Unlayered
 * outranks preflight + DaisyUI and still yields to a caller's inline `style`.
 *
 * SCOPE ROOT is the engine's outer `<div>`, which carries the pair
 * `ds-pattern-data-table ds-engine-modern` (plus a third `ds-table-density-*`
 * segment this skin never keys on) + `data-part='root'`. Every painted element
 * is a descendant with its own `data-part`. The card surface, the loading/empty
 * states, the pagination bar and the bulk bar are all descendants of that div.
 *
 * SPECIFICITY (P-48): the Platform-only Rottay artifact ships an unlayered
 * `html[data-tenant]:not([data-theme]):not(.light) *` at (0,3,1) that sets
 * `border-color` on every element. A descendant rule that paints `border` /
 * `border-color` / a `border-*-color` longhand must therefore reach (0,4,0):
 * the two root classes (0,2,0) + a second attribute on the target — the
 * `data-part` REPEATED (a legal double-count) or a contract
 * `data-variant`/`data-pinned`/`data-divider`/`data-last`. Rules that paint
 * only non-border channels (background, color, box-shadow, border-radius,
 * transform) beat preflight while unlayered at (0,3,0) and need no repeat. The
 * 4th unit is never bought from an incidental attribute (`role`, `aria-label`).
 * Pure `border: none` / `border-width`+`border-style` resets carry no color and
 * are exempt from the floor.
 *
 * Interaction paint the removed imperative row-hover handlers used to own now
 * lives here as ONE `:hover` rule, gated `[data-hoverable='true']:not(
 * [data-selected='true'])` — the exact `hoverable && !isSelected` guard the two
 * (grouped + flat) `onMouseEnter` handlers evaluated.
 *
 * Values are transcribed verbatim from `engines/modern.tsx`. The former
 * per-instance resize/sortable/focus/editable rules and keyframes now live in
 * the canonical `components/skin/data-table-interactions.css` recovery skin.
 */

/* ---- card surface ---- */
.ds-pattern-data-table.ds-engine-modern [data-part='card'] {
  background: var(--ds-table-bg, var(--ds-surface-card));
  border-radius: var(--ds-radius-lg);
