/**
 * Modern Textarea skin (WO-SKIN-02 checkpoint A, fields batch).
 *
 * DELIBERATELY UNLAYERED, same rationale as every other engine skin (P-47):
 * every `@layer rottay-*` sorts before Tailwind's `base` layer, so a layered
 * rule can't paint these elements at all; unlayered outranks preflight and
 * still yields to a caller's inline `style`.
 *
 * SCOPE ROOT is the `<textarea>` itself: `.ds-textarea.ds-textarea--modern
 * [data-part='root']`, carrying `data-variant` ('outlined'|'filled'|
 * 'borderless'), `data-status` ('default'|'error'|'warning'|'success') and
 * `data-disabled`.
 *
 * FOCUS is native `:focus`, not `:focus-visible`: `isFocused` is set
 * unconditionally in `onFocus`/`onBlur`, so the ring shows on any focus,
 * mouse or keyboard. The file's own JSDoc previously claimed ":focus-visible
 * only", which was stale relative to the actual handler and is corrected in
 * the same pass.
 *
 * BORDER COLOR reproduces the `computedBorderColor` chain: `variant=borderless`
 * resolves FIRST (-> transparent, wins over status and focus); otherwise a
 * focused, non-disabled field maps the DEFAULT status to primary while
 * error/warning/success keep their own color (identical focused or not, so
 * only default needs a focus override); at rest each status paints its own
 * color. Every non-borderless rule carries `:not([data-variant='borderless'])`
 * so at most one rule wins per (variant x status x focus) combination.
 *
 * BACKGROUND reproduces the `backgroundColor` chain: disabled (checked FIRST in
 * the JS) > filled > default. The disabled rule is ordered after filled so it
 * wins the (0,4,0) tie when a field is both.
 *
 * SPECIFICITY (P-48): the Platform-only Rottay artifact ships an unlayered
 * `html[data-tenant]:not([data-theme]):not(.light) *` border floor at (0,3,1);
 * every border-color rule below reaches (0,4,0) via a variant/status attribute
 * beyond the two root classes + `[data-part='root']`. Non-border paint
 * (background, color, outline, border-radius) wins unlayered at (0,3,0).
 */

.ds-textarea.ds-textarea--modern[data-part='root'] {
  color: var(--ds-color-text-primary);
  border-width: 1px;
  border-style: solid;
  border-radius: var(--ds-radius-md);
  background-color: var(--ds-color-bg-input, var(--ds-surface-control, transparent));
  outline: none;
}

/* background: filled, then disabled (disabled is checked first in the JS, so
   it is ordered last here to win the tie against filled). */
.ds-textarea.ds-textarea--modern[data-part='root'][data-variant='filled'] {
  background-color: var(--ds-color-bg-input, var(--ds-surface-control, var(--ds-color-bg-secondary)));
}
.ds-textarea.ds-textarea--modern[data-part='root'][data-disabled='true'] {
  color: var(--ds-color-text-disabled);
  background-color: var(--ds-color-bg-disabled, var(--ds-color-bg-secondary));
}

/* border color: borderless (transparent, wins over all), then per-status rest,
   then the default-status focus override. */
.ds-textarea.ds-textarea--modern[data-part='root'][data-variant='borderless'] {
  border-color: transparent;
}
.ds-textarea.ds-textarea--modern[data-part='root']:not([data-variant='borderless'])[data-status='default'] {
  border-color: var(--ds-color-border);
}
.ds-textarea.ds-textarea--modern[data-part='root']:not([data-variant='borderless'])[data-status='error'] {
  border-color: var(--ds-color-error);
}
.ds-textarea.ds-textarea--modern[data-part='root']:not([data-variant='borderless'])[data-status='warning'] {
  border-color: var(--ds-color-warning);
}
.ds-textarea.ds-textarea--modern[data-part='root']:not([data-variant='borderless'])[data-status='success'] {
  border-color: var(--ds-color-success);
}
.ds-textarea.ds-textarea--modern[data-part='root']:not([data-variant='borderless'])[data-status='default']:focus:not([data-disabled='true']) {
  border-color: var(--ds-color-primary);
}

/* Focus ring: base (status=default) + per-status override. `outline-offset`
   is constant across every branch; only the color channel varies. */
.ds-textarea.ds-textarea--modern[data-part='root']:focus:not([data-disabled='true']) {
  outline: 2px solid var(--ds-color-primary);
  outline-offset: -1px;
}
.ds-textarea.ds-textarea--modern[data-part='root']:focus:not([data-disabled='true'])[data-status='error'] {
  outline: 2px solid var(--ds-color-error);
  outline-offset: -1px;
}
.ds-textarea.ds-textarea--modern[data-part='root']:focus:not([data-disabled='true'])[data-status='warning'] {
  outline: 2px solid var(--ds-color-warning);
  outline-offset: -1px;
}
.ds-textarea.ds-textarea--modern[data-part='root']:focus:not([data-disabled='true'])[data-status='success'] {
  outline: 2px solid var(--ds-color-success);
  outline-offset: -1px;
}

/**
 * Rustic Textarea skin (WO-SKIN-02 checkpoint A, fields batch).
 *
 * DELIBERATELY UNLAYERED, same rationale as every other engine skin (P-47).
 *
 * SCOPE ROOT is the `<textarea>` itself: `.ds-textarea.ds-textarea--rustic
 * [data-part='root']`, carrying `data-status` and `data-disabled`. `variant`
 * ('outlined'|'filled'|'borderless') has no data-attribute but IS exposed as
 * a real rendered class, `rottay-textarea--${variant}`, unconditionally
 * present in the element's className -- used below instead of inventing new
 * anatomy.
 *
 * FOCUS is native `:focus`: `isFocused` (kept in local state only to feed
 * the `rottay-textarea--focused` external-override class hook, see the
 * component) is set unconditionally in onFocus/onBlur, matching `:focus`'s
 * semantics exactly.
 *
 * BORDER COLOR priority, transcribed byte-exact from the removed
 * `getBorderColor()`: status (error/warning/success) > focus > default;
 * `variant=borderless` overrides ALL of the above to `border: none`. Each
 * non-borderless rule below carries `:not(.rottay-textarea--borderless)` so
 * at most one rule ever wins per state (the P-48 guard idiom) rather than
 * relying on cascade order -- without it, the focus rule's extra `:not()`
 * chain would out-specify the borderless override.
 *
 * `count` (the optional char-counter div) is a DOM SIBLING of the root
 * textarea, not a descendant -- both are children of the wrapper div --
 * so it is selected via the general sibling combinator, which still lets it
 * carry the two root classes for the (0,3,0) floor.
 *
 * SPECIFICITY (P-48): `border` paints a color, so its rules reach (0,4,0)
 * via the repeated `[data-part='root']`. Every other rule here is
 * non-border paint and wins unlayered at (0,3,0).
 */

.ds-textarea.ds-textarea--rustic[data-part='root'] {
  outline: none;
  border-radius: var(--ds-textarea-radius);
  background-color: var(--ds-textarea-bg);
  color: var(--ds-textarea-color);
  box-shadow: none;
}

.ds-textarea.ds-textarea--rustic.rottay-textarea--filled[data-part='root']:not([data-disabled='true']) {
  background-color: var(--ds-textarea-filled-bg);
}

.ds-textarea.ds-textarea--rustic[data-part='root'][data-disabled='true'] {
  background-color: var(--ds-textarea-bg-disabled);
}

.ds-textarea.ds-textarea--rustic[data-part='root']:focus:not(.rottay-textarea--borderless) {
  box-shadow: var(--ds-textarea-shadow-focus);
}

/* border color: status > focus > default; borderless wins over all of them */
.ds-textarea.ds-textarea--rustic[data-part='root'][data-part='root'] {
  border: 1px solid var(--ds-textarea-border);
}
.ds-textarea.ds-textarea--rustic[data-part='root'][data-part='root']:focus:not(.rottay-textarea--borderless):not([data-status='error']):not([data-status='warning']):not([data-status='success']) {
  border: 1px solid var(--ds-textarea-border-focus);
}
.ds-textarea.ds-textarea--rustic[data-part='root'][data-part='root'][data-status='error']:not(.rottay-textarea--borderless) {
  border: 1px solid var(--ds-textarea-error-border);
}
.ds-textarea.ds-textarea--rustic[data-part='root'][data-part='root'][data-status='warning']:not(.rottay-textarea--borderless) {
  border: 1px solid var(--ds-textarea-warning-border);
}
.ds-textarea.ds-textarea--rustic[data-part='root'][data-part='root'][data-status='success']:not(.rottay-textarea--borderless) {
  border: 1px solid var(--ds-textarea-success-border);
}
.ds-textarea.ds-textarea--rustic.rottay-textarea--borderless[data-part='root'][data-part='root'] {
  border: none;
}

.ds-textarea.ds-textarea--rustic ~ [data-part='count'] {
  color: var(--ds-textarea-count-color);
}

/**
 * Modern TagInput skin (WO-SKIN-02 checkpoint A, fields batch).
 *
 * DELIBERATELY UNLAYERED, same rationale as every other engine skin (P-47):
 * every `@layer rottay-*` sorts before Tailwind's `base` layer, so a layered
 * rule can't paint these elements at all; unlayered outranks preflight and
 * still yields to a caller's inline `style`.
 *
 * SCOPE ROOT is `.ds-tag-input.ds-tag-input--modern[data-part='root']`,
 * carrying `data-error` ('true'|'false') and `data-disabled`. `tag-chip`,
 * `tag-remove`, and `input` are descendants of root. `error-message` is a
 * DOM NEPHEW of root, not a descendant: the JSX wraps it in an unclassed
 * `<div style={{marginTop:4}}>` that is itself a sibling of root (both
 * children of the component's outer wrapper) -- selected via the general
 * sibling combinator plus one descendant hop through that wrapper.
 *
 * This engine has no focus-driven paint at all (no `useInteractionState`,
 * no `isFocused`) -- the container's border only ever reacts to `data-error`.
 *
 * SPECIFICITY (P-48): the container's `border` paints a color, so its rules
 * reach (0,4,0) via the repeated `[data-part='root']`. Everything else here
 * is non-border paint (background, color, border-radius) and wins unlayered
 * at (0,3,0).
 */

.ds-tag-input.ds-tag-input--modern[data-part='root'] {
  border-radius: var(--ds-radius-md);
  background: var(--ds-color-bg-input);
}
.ds-tag-input.ds-tag-input--modern[data-part='root'][data-part='root'] {
  border: 1px solid var(--ds-color-border);
}
.ds-tag-input.ds-tag-input--modern[data-part='root'][data-part='root'][data-error='true'] {
  border: 1px solid var(--ds-color-error);
}

.ds-tag-input.ds-tag-input--modern [data-part='tag-chip'] {
  border-radius: 9999px;
  background: var(--ds-color-primary);
  color: var(--ds-color-text-on-primary);
}

.ds-tag-input.ds-tag-input--modern [data-part='tag-remove'] {
  background: transparent;
  color: inherit;
  border: none;
}

.ds-tag-input.ds-tag-input--modern [data-part='input'] {
  outline: none;
  background: transparent;
  border: none;
}

.ds-tag-input.ds-tag-input--modern ~ * [data-part='error-message'] {
  color: var(--ds-color-error);
}

/**
 * Rustic TagInput skin (WO-SKIN-02 checkpoint A, fields batch).
 *
 * DELIBERATELY UNLAYERED, same rationale as every other engine skin (P-47).
 *
 * SCOPE ROOT is `.ds-tag-input.ds-tag-input--rustic[data-part='root']`,
 * carrying `data-error` and `data-disabled`. `error-message` IS a direct DOM
 * sibling of root here (no intermediate wrapper, unlike the modern engine)
 * -- selected via a plain general sibling combinator.
 *
 * FOCUS: the removed `useInteractionState()` call's `focused` (read only to
 * drive the border/box-shadow this skin now paints) was set exclusively by
 * `onFocus`/`onBlur` spread onto `[data-part='input']` -- never onto the
 * tag-remove buttons -- so it tracked ONLY that one descendant's native
 * focus (interaction-state's own doc: "`focused` is any focus"). A plain
 * `:focus-within` on root would also fire when a remove button is
 * tab-focused, which the removed state never did; `:has([data-part='input']
 * :focus)` reproduces the original scope exactly.
 *
 * BORDER COLOR priority, byte-exact from the removed inline ternary:
 * error > focused > default. `box-shadow` (the focus ring) has no error
 * dependency -- it shows on focus regardless of error state, matching the
 * original.
 *
 * SPECIFICITY (P-48): border paints a color, so its rules reach (0,4,0) via
 * the repeated `[data-part='root']`. Everything else here is non-border
 * paint (background, color, box-shadow, border-radius) and wins unlayered
 * at (0,3,0).
 *
 * Fallback literals (`#ef4444`, `#3b82f6`, `#d1d5db`, `#f3f4f6`, `#fff`,
 * `#dbeafe`, `#1d4ed8`, `rgba(59, 130, 246, 0.2)`) are transcribed
 * byte-exact from the source `var(--ds-color-*, #hex)` declarations.
 */

.ds-tag-input.ds-tag-input--rustic[data-part='root'] {
  border-radius: 8px;
  background-color: var(--ds-color-bg-input, #fff);
  box-shadow: none;
}
.ds-tag-input.ds-tag-input--rustic[data-part='root'][data-disabled='true'] {
  background-color: var(--ds-color-neutral-100, #f3f4f6);
}
.ds-tag-input.ds-tag-input--rustic[data-part='root']:has([data-part='input']:focus) {
  box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px var(--ds-color-primary-100, rgba(59, 130, 246, 0.2));
}

.ds-tag-input.ds-tag-input--rustic[data-part='root'][data-part='root'] {
  border: 1px solid var(--ds-color-neutral-300, #d1d5db);
}
.ds-tag-input.ds-tag-input--rustic[data-part='root'][data-part='root']:has([data-part='input']:focus):not([data-error='true']) {
  border: 1px solid var(--ds-color-primary-500, #3b82f6);
}
.ds-tag-input.ds-tag-input--rustic[data-part='root'][data-part='root'][data-error='true'] {
  border: 1px solid var(--ds-color-error-500, #ef4444);
}

.ds-tag-input.ds-tag-input--rustic [data-part='tag-chip'] {
  background-color: var(--ds-color-primary-100, #dbeafe);
  color: var(--ds-color-primary-700, #1d4ed8);
  border-radius: 4px;
}

.ds-tag-input.ds-tag-input--rustic [data-part='tag-remove'] {
  border: none;
  background: transparent;
  color: inherit;
}

.ds-tag-input.ds-tag-input--rustic [data-part='input'] {
  border: none;
  outline: none;
  background: transparent;
}

.ds-tag-input.ds-tag-input--rustic ~ [data-part='error-message'] {
  color: var(--ds-color-error-500, #ef4444);
}

/**
 * Modern InputNumber skin (WO-SKIN-02 checkpoint A, fields batch).
 *
 * DELIBERATELY UNLAYERED, same rationale as every other engine skin (P-47):
 * every `@layer rottay-*` sorts before Tailwind's `base` layer, so a layered
 * rule can't paint these elements at all; unlayered outranks preflight and
 * still yields to a caller's inline `style`.
 *
 * SCOPE ROOT is `.ds-input-number.ds-input-number--modern[data-part='root']`,
 * the `<input>` itself -- carrying `data-status` ('default'|'error'|'warning')
 * and `data-disabled`. Unlike a container-root component (TagInput, Textarea),
 * a void `<input>` cannot have descendants, so every other part
 * (`addon-before`, `prefix`, `suffix`, `stepper-button`, `addon-after`) is a
 * SIBLING or NEPHEW of root, not a child -- some of them (`addon-before`,
 * `prefix`) precede root in the DOM, which a forward-only `~`/descendant
 * combinator anchored ON root cannot reach. Each such part is instead
 * anchored on ITSELF and reaches forward with `:has()` to confirm it shares
 * the component's wrapper (`[part]:has(~ … root)`); parts that follow root
 * are still reached the ordinary way (`root ~ …`). This reproduces the exact
 * JSX nesting (`<div addon-before?><div middle><span prefix?><input root>
 * <div><span suffix?><div stepper?></div></div></div><div addon-after?>`)
 * so no rule can bleed into an unrelated component that happens to reuse the
 * same `data-part` name elsewhere on the page.
 *
 * This engine has no focus-driven paint (no `useInteractionState`) -- the
 * root's border only ever reacts to `data-status`.
 *
 * SPECIFICITY (P-48): the root's `border` paints a color, so its rules reach
 * (0,4,0) via the repeated `[data-part='root']`. Everything else here is
 * non-border paint (background, color, outline, border-radius) and wins
 * unlayered at (0,3,0) or higher.
 */

.ds-input-number.ds-input-number--modern[data-part='root'] {
  background: var(--ds-color-bg-input, var(--ds-surface-control));
  color: var(--ds-color-text-primary);
  outline: none;
  border-radius: var(--ds-radius-md);
}

.ds-input-number.ds-input-number--modern[data-part='root'][data-part='root'] {
  border: 1px solid var(--ds-color-border);
}
.ds-input-number.ds-input-number--modern[data-part='root'][data-part='root'][data-status='error'] {
  border: 1px solid var(--ds-color-error);
}
.ds-input-number.ds-input-number--modern[data-part='root'][data-part='root'][data-status='warning'] {
  border: 1px solid var(--ds-color-warning);
}

[data-part='addon-before']:has(~ div > .ds-input-number.ds-input-number--modern[data-part='root']) {
  background: var(--ds-surface-inset);
}
div:has(> .ds-input-number.ds-input-number--modern[data-part='root']) ~ [data-part='addon-after'] {
