 * local state ONLY to drive the `rottay-inputnumber--focused` external class
 * hook on the outer wrapper (non-paint, untouched) -- its own `onFocus`/
 * `onBlur` handlers are spread exclusively onto `[data-part='root']`, so
 * native `:focus` on root reproduces the removed paint exactly.
 *
 * BORDER COLOR priority, byte-exact from the removed `getBorderColor()`:
 * error > warning > focused > default. `box-shadow` (the focus ring) has no
 * status dependency -- it shows on focus regardless of status, matching the
 * original (`isFocused ? shadow-focus : 'none'`, no status branch).
 *
 * BORDER-RADIUS is genuinely prop-derived (depends on whether `addonBefore`/
 * `addonAfter` are present, which stamp no anatomy of their own to key a CSS
 * selector on) -- carried via the quoted custom property
 * `--ds-input-number-radius`, set inline (uncounted) from the SAME ternary
 * the JSX always computed, consumed here by a static rule.
 *
 * SPECIFICITY (P-48): border paints a color, so its rules reach (0,4,0) via
 * the repeated `[data-part='root']`. Everything else here is non-border
 * paint (background, color, box-shadow, border-radius) and wins unlayered at
 * (0,3,0) or higher.
