 * root); `strength-track` and `error-message` are nephews (siblings of root's
 * own parent), reached by anchoring on that parent via `div:has(> root) ~ …`.
 *
 * BORDER reproduces the `inputStyle`/`getBorderColor` chain: outlined/filled
 * get a 1px box border, flushed only a 2px bottom edge, unstyled none; in
 * every case the edge color follows error > focus > default. The box-border
 * rules carry `:not([data-variant='flushed']):not([data-variant='unstyled'])`
 * mirroring the JS variant ternary so at most one border rule wins per
 * (variant x error x focus) combination.
 *
 * FOCUS: `isFocused` (set unconditionally in onFocus/onBlur on root) matched
 * native `:focus` exactly; `box-shadow` reproduces `isFocused && !error` via
 * `:focus:not([data-error='true'])`.
 *
 * SPECIFICITY (P-48): the Platform-only Rottay artifact ships an unlayered border floor at (0,3,1);
 * every border-color rule below reaches (0,4,0) via a variant/error attribute
 * (or `:not()` chain) beyond the two root classes + `[data-part='root']`.
 * Non-border paint (background, color, outline, box-shadow, border-radius)
 * wins unlayered at (0,3,0) or higher.
 *
 * Fallback literals (`#1a1a1a`, `#666`, `#d9d9d9`, `#1890ff`, `#ff4d4f`,
 * `#f5f5f5`, `#e8e8e8`, `rgba(24, 144, 255, 0.2)`) are transcribed byte-exact
 * from the source `var(--ds-color-*, #hex)` declarations.
 */

.ds-password-input.ds-password-input--rustic[data-part='root'] {
  color: var(--ds-color-text-primary, #1a1a1a);
  outline: none;
  box-shadow: none;
}
.ds-password-input.ds-password-input--rustic[data-part='root']:focus:not([data-error='true']) {
  box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px var(--ds-color-primary-100, rgba(24, 144, 255, 0.2));
}

/* background: filled tint, else transparent. */
