 * modifier (added here to `ds-upload`/`ds-upload-dragger` too, and to rustic's
 * Dragger root, which lacked it -- see the rustic skin header), every root
 * additionally carries `ds-upload--${listType}` / `ds-upload-dragger--${listType}`
 * when `listType !== 'text'` (text has no modifier, matching rustic).
 *
 * SPECIFICITY (P-48): the Platform-only Rottay artifact ships an unlayered border-color floor at
 * (0,3,1). Every rule that paints a border COLOR here reaches (0,4,0) via a
 * listType root modifier class, or (where no modifier applies) a repeated
 * `[data-part='x'][data-part='x']`. Non-border paint (background, color,
 * box-shadow, outline, border-radius) wins unlayered at (0,3,0) or higher.
 *
 * The progress-bar fill is a runtime `progress.strokeColor` (plain color or a
 * computed `linear-gradient(...)`), carried via the uncounted custom property
 * `--ds-upload-progress-fill` and consumed by the rule below; only the runtime
 * `width` stays inline.
 *
 * DEVIATION (reported, not silently taken):
 * 2. The Dragger's active-drag paint (`border-primary bg-primary/5 shadow-lg
 *    scale-[1.01]`, applied via conditional Tailwind utility classes, not an
 *    object-literal style key) is NOT counted by the inline-paint audit and is
 *    left in the JSX untouched -- `Upload.engine-advanced.test.tsx:135`
 *    asserts `border-primary` is present in the dropzone's className during
 *    drag, and this repo ships no `tailwind.config.*` this agent could read to
 *    verify the exact compiled value of an opacity-modified utility
 *    (`bg-primary/5`) or `shadow-lg`, so duplicating them into a static CSS
 *    rule risked a byte-INEXACT transcription -- a worse RULE ZERO violation
 *    than leaving a harmless, already-correct mechanism alone. Only the
 *    genuinely counted inline site -- the inactive-state `borderColor`
 *    conditional -- moves to CSS below, keyed on the idle branch of the
 *    pre-existing `data-state='dragging'|'idle'` attribute so it cannot fight
 *    the still-Tailwind-driven dragging-state border color.
