 *   migration -- both were Tailwind-only passthrough -- so this migration adds
 *   `rottay-timepicker`/`rottay-timepicker--modern` (single) and
 *   `rottay-timepicker-range`/`rottay-timepicker-range--modern` (range),
 *   mirroring the BEM family the rustic engine already carries for this same
 *   component (not a `ds-` prefix).
 * - `TimePanel` (the hour/minute/second dropdown) is `createPortal(...,
 *   document.body)` -- it is NOT a DOM descendant of the trigger root, so it
 *   cannot be scoped under the trigger's class. It carried only
 *   `data-part='panel'` with no class; this migration adds the self-sufficient
 *   `rottay-timepicker__panel` class so panel rules can scope standalone,
 *   mirroring ColorPicker rustic's `rottay-colorpicker__dropdown`. `TimePanel`
 *   is shared verbatim by `TimePickerBase` and `TimeRangePicker`, so one panel
 *   ruleset serves both.
 *
 * STATUS: neither trigger root carried a status/disabled modifier class
 * pre-migration (unlike the rustic engine's BEM modifiers) -- the border-color
 * override was pure inline JS keyed on the `status` prop. This migration adds
 * `data-status` ('default'|'error'|'warning') to each trigger-input, the same
 * discriminator idiom InputNumber's modern skin uses.
 *
 * ACTIVE RANGE INPUT: `TimeRangePicker`'s start/end box-shadow ring was never
 * native focus -- it painted whichever input `activeInput` currently targets
 * while the panel is open. `data-active` (added here) reproduces the removed
 * inline ternary's condition exactly: `activeInput === 'start' && isOpen`
 * (and the `'end'` counterpart).
 *
 * KEYFRAME: `rottay-select-slide-in` was injected per-mount via a `<style>`
 * tag inside `TimePanel` itself. Renamed `ds-time-picker-slide-in` and moved
 * here (loads once, globally, instead of re-injecting on every panel mount);
 * `TimePanel`'s inline `animation` reference was updated to match.
 *
 * SPECIFICITY (P-48): the Platform-only Rottay artifact ships an unlayered
 * `html[data-tenant]:not([data-theme]):not(.light) *` border-color floor at
 * (0,3,1). Under the trigger root, a border-color rule reaches (0,4,0) via the
 * two root classes + the target's own `data-part` repeated, same as every
 * other engine skin. Under the standalone panel there is no root PAIR to draw
 * on, so the single `rottay-timepicker__panel` class is repeated twice in its
 * place, plus the target's own `data-part` repeated twice -- matching
 * ColorPicker rustic's `.dropdown.dropdown [data-part='x'][data-part='x']`
 * idiom. Non-border paint (background, color, box-shadow, outline,
 * border-radius) and pure `border: none` resets win unlayered at (0,3,0) or a
 * single class.
 */

/* ---- trigger (in-tree): base + range share identical rest-state paint ---- */

.rottay-timepicker.rottay-timepicker--modern [data-part='trigger-input'],
.rottay-timepicker-range.rottay-timepicker-range--modern [data-part='trigger-input'] {
  border-radius: var(--ds-radius-md);
  background: var(--ds-color-bg-input, var(--ds-surface-control));
  color: var(--ds-color-text-primary);
  outline: none;
}

.rottay-timepicker.rottay-timepicker--modern [data-part='trigger-input'][data-part='trigger-input'],
.rottay-timepicker-range.rottay-timepicker-range--modern [data-part='trigger-input'][data-part='trigger-input'] {
  border: 1px solid var(--ds-color-border);
}
.rottay-timepicker.rottay-timepicker--modern [data-part='trigger-input'][data-part='trigger-input'][data-status='error'],
.rottay-timepicker-range.rottay-timepicker-range--modern [data-part='trigger-input'][data-part='trigger-input'][data-status='error'] {
  border-color: var(--ds-color-error);
}
.rottay-timepicker.rottay-timepicker--modern [data-part='trigger-input'][data-part='trigger-input'][data-status='warning'],
.rottay-timepicker-range.rottay-timepicker-range--modern [data-part='trigger-input'][data-part='trigger-input'][data-status='warning'] {
  border-color: var(--ds-color-warning);
}

.rottay-timepicker-range.rottay-timepicker-range--modern [data-part='trigger-input'][data-active='true'] {
  box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px var(--ds-color-primary);
}

.rottay-timepicker-range.rottay-timepicker-range--modern [data-part='separator'] {
  color: var(--ds-color-text-secondary);
}

/* ---- clear-button / clock-icon: `TimePickerBase` only -- `TimeRangePicker`
        renders neither. ---- */

.rottay-timepicker.rottay-timepicker--modern [data-part='clear-button'] {
  transform: translateY(-50%);
  background: none;
  border: none;
  border-radius: 50%;
  color: var(--ds-color-text-primary);
}

.rottay-timepicker.rottay-timepicker--modern [data-part='clock-icon'] {
  transform: translateY(-50%);
  color: var(--ds-color-text-muted);
