 * state they share, so one `[data-part='cell']` ruleset below serves all
 * three -- discriminated only by state attributes already stamped (`data-
 * today`, `data-selected`, `data-in-range`), which month/year cells simply
 * never carry `data-in-range` on.
 *
 * TWO NEW STATE ATTRIBUTES (not in the pre-existing BEM contract, added here
 * because their JS drove real counted paint with no attribute to key on):
 * - `data-outside-month`: `getCellStyle`'s `color` ternary branched on
 *   `!cell.isCurrentMonth` (padding days from the adjacent month render
 *   dimmer) -- a real color dependency, unlike the modern engine, where the
 *   equivalent state only ever drove `opacity` (uncounted). Maps 1:1 to
 *   `!cell.isCurrentMonth`, stamped only on the day-grid cell.
 * - `data-focused`: `getCellStyle`'s `border` ternary's second branch keyed
 *   on the keyboard-nav "focused cell" (`isFocusedCell`, from `focusedDate`)
 *   -- a roving-tabindex target, NOT real DOM `:focus` (no `.focus()` call
 *   exists anywhere in this file for grid cells), so a `:focus` pseudo-class
 *   cannot reproduce it. Maps 1:1 to `isFocusedCell`, stamped only on the
 *   day-grid cell. Priority vs. the today-ring is preserved via the
 *   `:not([data-today='true']), […][data-selected='true']` OR-split below
 *   (see the two-selector focus-ring rule), matching the original ternary's
 *   `isToday && !isSelected && !isEndpoint ? todayRing : isFocused ?
 *   focusRing : none` exactly (`isEndpoint` folded into `data-selected`).
 *
 * ACTIVE RANGE INPUT: `RangePicker`'s start/end border+box-shadow ring was
 * never real DOM focus -- `getBorderColor(status, activeInput === inputType
 * && isOpen)` painted whichever input `activeInput` currently targets while
 * the panel is open (no `onFocus`/`onBlur` on these inputs at all). `data-
 * active` (added here) reproduces that condition exactly, replacing
 * `isFocused` as the third priority tier in the border-color cascade (see
 * STATUS PRIORITY below) -- same idiom as the modern engine's own
 * `data-active`, and as TimePicker modern's range input.
 *
 * FOCUS (single trigger only): the paint (border color, box-shadow) applies
 * directly to `[data-part='trigger-input']`, the SAME element that receives
 * native focus -- not a container painting for a nested input -- so a plain
 * `:focus` pseudo-class reproduces the removed `useInteractionState()`/
 * `isFocused`-driven paint exactly, with no React-render-timing gap.
 * `DatePickerBase` keeps `useInteractionState()`; its `focused` flag still
 * drives the `rottay-datepicker--focused` root modifier class, unrelated to
 * paint (RangePicker has no such state at all -- it never had a `--focused`
 * modifier, only `data-active` above).
 *
 * STATUS PRIORITY: error > warning > focused/active > default, matching the
 * removed `getBorderColor()` priority chain byte-exact. The focus/active
 * border rule is guarded with `:not(...--error):not(...--warning)` so a
 * status root modifier always outranks it, regardless of selector order. The
 * box-shadow ring has no status dependency in the original -- it shows
 * regardless of status, so it carries no such guard.
 *
 * DAY-GRID CELL HOVER: the removed `onMouseEnter`/`onMouseLeave` applied
 * `transform: scale(1.1)` unconditionally for any non-disabled cell
 * (including selected/endpoint ones), but only repainted `backgroundColor`
 * when NOT selected/endpoint -- an asymmetric guard, preserved exactly below
 * (two separate `:hover` rules, transform ungated, background gated). The
 * leave-state resets to the resting value the rules above already provide.
 *
 * SPECIFICITY (P-48): the Platform-only Rottay artifact ships an unlayered
 * `html[data-tenant]:not([data-theme]):not(.light) *` border-color floor at
 * (0,3,1). Under a trigger root, a border-color rule reaches (0,4,0) via the
 * two root classes + the target's own `data-part` repeated. Under the
 * standalone panel there is no trigger root pair to draw on, so the panel's
 * own class pair plays that role, plus the target's own `data-part`
 * repeated -- matching the modern engine's identical panel idiom. Non-border
 * paint (background-color, color, box-shadow, outline, border-radius) and
 * pure `border: none`/`background: none` resets win unlayered at (0,3,0) or
 * lower.
 */

/* ---- trigger (in-tree): single ---- */

.rottay-datepicker.rottay-datepicker--rustic [data-part='trigger-input'] {
  border-radius: var(--ds-datepicker-radius, 8px);
  outline: none;
  background-color: var(--ds-datepicker-bg, var(--ds-color-bg-elevated));
  color: var(--ds-datepicker-color, var(--ds-color-text-primary));
  box-shadow: none;
}
.rottay-datepicker.rottay-datepicker--rustic [data-part='trigger-input']:disabled {
  background-color: var(--ds-datepicker-bg-disabled, var(--ds-color-bg-secondary));
}
.rottay-datepicker.rottay-datepicker--rustic [data-part='trigger-input']:focus {
  box-shadow: var(--ds-datepicker-shadow-focus, 0 0 0 3px var(--ds-color-primary-100), 0 0 8px var(--ds-color-primary-200));
}

.rottay-datepicker.rottay-datepicker--rustic [data-part='trigger-input'][data-part='trigger-input'] {
  border: 1px solid var(--ds-datepicker-border, var(--ds-color-border));
}
.rottay-datepicker.rottay-datepicker--rustic:not(.rottay-datepicker--error):not(.rottay-datepicker--warning) [data-part='trigger-input'][data-part='trigger-input']:focus {
  border: 1px solid var(--ds-datepicker-border-focus, var(--ds-color-primary-500));
}
.rottay-datepicker.rottay-datepicker--rustic.rottay-datepicker--error [data-part='trigger-input'][data-part='trigger-input'] {
  border: 1px solid var(--ds-datepicker-error-border, var(--ds-color-error));
}
.rottay-datepicker.rottay-datepicker--rustic.rottay-datepicker--warning [data-part='trigger-input'][data-part='trigger-input'] {
  border: 1px solid var(--ds-datepicker-warning-border, var(--ds-color-warning));
}

.rottay-datepicker.rottay-datepicker--rustic [data-part='clear-button'] {
  background: none;
  border: none;
  color: var(--ds-datepicker-clear-color, var(--ds-color-text-tertiary));
}

.rottay-datepicker.rottay-datepicker--rustic [data-part='calendar-icon'] {
  color: var(--ds-datepicker-icon-color, var(--ds-color-text-tertiary));
}

/* ---- trigger (in-tree): range ---- */

.rottay-datepicker-range.rottay-datepicker-range--rustic [data-part='trigger-input'] {
  border-radius: var(--ds-datepicker-radius, 8px);
  outline: none;
  background-color: var(--ds-datepicker-bg, var(--ds-color-bg-elevated));
  color: var(--ds-datepicker-color, var(--ds-color-text-primary));
