/**
 * Modern TreeSelect skin (WO-SKIN-02 checkpoint B, dropdown family).
 *
 * DELIBERATELY UNLAYERED, same rationale as every other engine skin (P-47):
 * every `rottay-*` layer sorts before Tailwind's `base` layer, so a layered
 * rule loses to preflight regardless of specificity. Unlayered outranks
 * preflight + DaisyUI and still yields to a caller's inline `style`.
 *
 * SCOPE ROOT is the outer `<div>`, which now carries the pair
 * `ds-tree-select ds-tree-select--modern` + `data-part='root'` (stamped by
 * this migration -- the pre-step had left the root component-scope-class-
 * free, unlike Select's root). The trigger, dropdown, tree list, and every
 * node row are IN-TREE descendants with their own `data-part` (TreeSelect
 * modern never portals -- the mirror image of Select, whose custom-dropdown
 * branch does).
 *
 * SPECIFICITY (P-48): the Platform-only Rottay artifact ships an unlayered `*` border floor at
 * (0,3,1); a rule that sets a border COLOR must reach (0,4,0). The two root
 * classes (0,2,0) + `[data-part='root']` + any descendant `[data-part]`
 * already reach (0,4,0) with a single descendant hop, so no part here needs
 * the repeated-`[data-part]` trick.
 *
 * The tree-node row's selected background/color/border-left and the
 * tree-line indent's border-left are transcribed verbatim from
 * `engines/modern.tsx` (both were plain conditional inline styles -- this
 * file has no imperative `.style.` writes anywhere). `treeLine` (a static
 * per-instance prop, not per-node) is threaded onto the recursive child
 * `<ul>` as `data-tree-line` so CSS can key off it; the outer (non-recursive)
 * tree list never carried a border regardless of `treeLine` and is left
 * unmatched.
 *
 * KEYFRAMES: `@keyframes rottay-select-slide-in`, previously an inline
 * `<style dangerouslySetInnerHTML>` re-injected on every open, is moved here
 * renamed `ds-tree-select-slide-in`; the dropdown's `animation:` reference
 * (an inline, non-paint key) is updated to match. The loading spinner's bare
 * `animation: 'spin …'` has no local `@keyframes` in the source and resolves
 * against the global foundation `spin` keyframe -- left inline, untouched.
 */

@keyframes ds-tree-select-slide-in {
  from {
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(-4px) scale(0.98);
  }
  to {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: translateY(0) scale(1);
  }
}

