/**
 * Modern Cascader skin (WO-SKIN-02 checkpoint B, dropdown family).
 *
 * DELIBERATELY UNLAYERED, same rationale as every other engine skin (P-47):
 * every `rottay-*` layer sorts before Tailwind's `base` layer, so a layered
 * rule loses to preflight regardless of specificity. Unlayered outranks
 * preflight + DaisyUI and still yields to a caller's inline `style`.
 *
 * SCOPE ROOT is the outer `<div>`, which now carries the pair
 * `ds-cascader ds-cascader--modern` (stamped by this migration -- the
 * pre-step had left the root component-scope-class-free, like TreeSelect's
 * root) alongside its pre-existing `data-part='root'`. **NO PORTAL**: the
 * trigger, dropdown, search input, columns, and every option row are IN-TREE
 * descendants of the root with their own `data-part` (grep-verified -- this
 * file has no `createPortal` import, unlike the rustic sibling below).
 *
 * SPECIFICITY (P-48): the Platform-only Rottay artifact ships an unlayered `*` border floor at
 * (0,3,1); a rule that sets a border COLOR must reach (0,4,0). The two root
 * classes (0,2,0) + `[data-part='root']` + any descendant `[data-part]`
 * already reach (0,4,0) with a single descendant hop, so nothing here needs
 * the repeated-`[data-part]` trick, including selectors that add a further
 * `:not()`/state attribute (they only exceed the floor further).
 *
 * Every value below is transcribed verbatim from `engines/modern.tsx`'s
 * inline `style={{...}}` objects -- this file has zero imperative `.style.`
 * writes (grep-confirmed), so there is no hover-handler deletion to record.
 *
 * RE-STAMPED DATA-PART: the cascading menu columns (`data-part='menu-column'`)
 * conditionally painted a `borderRight` only when `colIndex < activeColumns.
 * length - 1` ("not the last column") -- a runtime boolean with no existing
 * DOM hook. A new `data-last` boolean attribute (`colIndex === activeColumns.
 * length - 1 || undefined`, mirroring this file's existing `data-open`/
 * `data-selected` idiom) was added to the `<ul data-part='menu-column'>` so
 * CSS can key off it; `menu-column` itself is unchanged (it is one of the
 * contract-test-pinned parts).
 *
 * KEYFRAMES: the conditional `<style dangerouslySetInnerHTML>` (mounted only
 * while `isOpen`) defined two keyframes consumed by two different elements --
 * `rottay-select-slide-in` (the dropdown panel's entrance) and
 * `rottay-cascader-panel-in` (each non-first column's entrance, `colIndex >
 * 0`). Both are moved here renamed `ds-cascader-slide-in` /
 * `ds-cascader-panel-in`; the `<style>` tag is deleted and both inline
 * `animation:` references (non-paint keys, left inline) are updated to match.
 * The loading spinner's bare `animation: 'spin ...'` has no local `@keyframes`
 * in the source and resolves against the global foundation `spin` keyframe --
 * left inline, untouched.
 *
 * WON'T-TRANSCRIBE / NOT INVENTED: the option row's dead `active`/`disabled`
 * className tokens (no in-file stylesheet target) and the search-mode result
 * row (zero paint in source) are preserved exactly as-is -- no CSS invented
 * for either.
 */

@keyframes ds-cascader-slide-in {
  from {
    opacity: 0;
