/* Overlay family (WO-SKIN-03 checkpoint O). */
/**
 * Modern Modal skin (WO-SKIN-03 checkpoint O).
 *
 * DELIBERATELY UNLAYERED (P-47): every `rottay-*` layer sorts before Tailwind's
 * base layer, so a layered rule loses to preflight regardless of specificity.
 * Unlayered outranks preflight and still yields to a caller's inline `style`.
 *
 * SPECIFICITY (P-48): every rule painting a border COLOR reaches b >= 4 to clear
 * the tenant artifacts' unlayered `html[data-tenant]:not([data-theme]):not(.light) *`
 * border-color floor at (0,3,1). Bought from the root class repeated plus the
 * target's own repeated `data-part`. Color-free resets (`border: none`,
 * `outline: none`) are exempt from that floor.
 *
 * PORTAL: both engines mount through the shared Portal utility into
 * `#rottay-portal-root` on `document.body`, outside any tenant-scoped subtree.
 * Every selector here is therefore anchored on the component's own root class
 * and resolves anywhere in the document (the Select dropdown-panel precedent).
 *
 * PERSONALITY: runtime/personality.css keys its modal rules on `.ant-modal`,
 * `.modal`, `.modal-backdrop`, `.modal-box` and `[data-engine] .ds-modal*`.
 * This engine carries none of those classes, so no personality rule matches any
 * element painted here -- neither before nor after the migration.
 *
 * DIRECT-CHILD COMBINATORS are load-bearing: `Modal.Header`/`Body`/`Footer`/
 * `CloseButton` compounds re-use the same `data-part` names and can be composed
 * INSIDE this engine's body. Anchoring each section rule on `surface > ...`
 * keeps engine paint off a composed compound, which owns its own skin.
