 * SPECIFICITY (P-48): the only rule here that paints a border COLOR is the
 * loading spinner's ring, and it reaches exactly b=4 (class + data-tone +
 * data-part + `:empty`), clearing the tenant artifacts' unlayered
 * `html[data-tenant]:not([data-theme]):not(.light) *` border-color floor at
 * (0,3,1). `border: none` on the close button is a color-free reset and is exempt.
 *
 * The stacking container is the external DaisyUI `.toast` class; `theme.css`'s
 * `[data-tenant] .toast` rule references six `--ds-toast-*` tokens that are
 * declared nowhere, leaving that container functionally unstyled. That is
 * untouched here -- the container had no inline paint to migrate.
 */

