/**
 * Modern AlertDialog skin (WO-SKIN-04 checkpoint P).
 *
 * DELIBERATELY UNLAYERED (P-47): every `@layer rottay-*` sorts before Tailwind's
 * base layer, so a layered rule cannot paint these elements at all.
 *
 * THIS ENGINE'S DaisyUI CLASSES ARE LOAD-BEARING AND MUST NOT BE REMOVED (P2a).
 * It is the only component in this family that renders real DaisyUI structural
 * classes (`modal modal-open`, `modal-backdrop`, `modal-box`, `modal-action`), and
 * TWO of its shipping paint channels have no inline footprint at all — they are
 * painted entirely by `runtime/personality.css` (layer `rottay-personality`):
 *
 *   .modal-backdrop { backdrop-filter: blur(4px); -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(4px); }
 *   .modal-box      { box-shadow: 0 25px 50px -12px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.25); }
 *
 * Personality's layer sorts AFTER `rottay-engines`, so it also outranks
 * `modern/theme.css`'s own `[data-tenant] .modal-box { box-shadow: … }`. This file
 * therefore declares NEITHER `box-shadow` NOR `backdrop-filter` on those two parts:
 * an unlayered rule here would outrank personality and silently replace a shipping
 * blur and shadow. They stay externally sourced, exactly as they ship.
 *
 * `background` and `border-radius` DO move here. They were inline before (inline
 * outranks every layer) and are unlayered now (which also outranks every layer), so
 * the winner's value is unchanged — they still mask `theme.css`'s `.modal-box`
 * background/radius declarations, as they always did.
 *
 * PORTAL: this engine does NOT portal (neither does rustic) — the tree renders
 * in-tree as a `position: fixed` sibling. The scope class still anchors every rule,
 * so the selectors are position-independent.
 *
 * SCOPE: `rottay-alert-dialog--modern`. NOT `ds-popover` / `ds-dropdown` — those two
 * names carry DORMANT entrance-animation rules in personality.css that match nothing
 * today (P3); adopting either would hand this component an animation it has never had.
 */

.rottay-alert-dialog--modern[data-part='root'] > [data-part='backdrop'] {
  background: var(--ds-overlay-bg);
}

.rottay-alert-dialog--modern[data-part='root'] > [data-part='surface'] {
