 * `border-right: none` rules therefore have to out-rank the shorthand that
 * precedes them: they carry at least the same (0,4,0) and come later, so they
 * win on `border-right-style` exactly as the inline spread order did.
 *
 * SPECIFICITY (P-48): the shared `border` shorthand carries a real color and
 * must clear the tenant's unlayered `* { border-color }` floor at (0,3,1), so it
 * reaches (0,4,0) via the scope class + the root attr + a REPEATED `data-part`
 * on the target (a compound, no descendant space), and stays a SHORTHAND.
 * `border-right: none` is a color-free reset (exempt from the floor) but is held
 * at (0,4,0)+ so it still beats the shorthand. `background` / `color` /
