/**
 * Modern Segmented skin (WO-SKIN-04 checkpoint N).
 *
 * DELIBERATELY UNLAYERED (P-47): every `rottay-*` layer sorts before Tailwind's
 * base layer, so a layered rule cannot paint these elements at all. Unlayered
 * still yields to a caller's inline `style`.
 *
 * NO DaisyUI HERE, despite the file's own header comment: modern Segmented's
 * doc block claims it "uses DaisyUI's `join` component", but the render carries
 * zero DaisyUI classes — the same stale claim Pagination's header makes. There
 * is no `join`/`btn` hook to preserve and no `theme.css` block to reconcile
 * against; this is a clean greenfield skin.
 *
 * SCOPE ROOT carries `rottay-segmented rottay-segmented--modern` +
 * `data-part='root'`; each option button carries `data-part='option'` +
 * `data-selected` + `data-disabled`. Option rules are anchored under the root
 * scope — `option` is shared vocabulary and must never be matched bare.
 *
 * SPECIFICITY (P-48): the root's `border` shorthand carries a real color, so it
 * must clear the tenant's unlayered `* { border-color }` floor at (0,3,1) — it
 * reaches (0,4,0) via the two scope classes + a repeated `data-part`, and stays
 * a SHORTHAND. The option's `border: none` is a color-free reset, exempt. The
