/**
 * Rustic Calendar skin (WO-SKIN-05 checkpoint D2).
 *
 * DELIBERATELY UNLAYERED (P-47): a layered rule sorts before Tailwind's base
 * layer and loses to preflight; unlayered outranks preflight and still yields to
 * the caller's inline `style`.
 *
 * SCOPE ROOT carries `rottay-calendar rottay-calendar--rustic` + `data-part` +
 * `data-mode` (grep-verified free: Calendar was fully greenfield -- no
 * first-party classname, no theme.css bridge, no personality hook, in either
 * engine). The engine suffix is load-bearing: modern carries the same base class
 * and paints different values.
 *
 * HOVER WAS REACT STATE. A single `hovered: string | null` was compared against
 * each element's key and spread into its style object on match; the `:hover`
 * rules below reproduce all six sites (four nav arrows, day cell, month cell),
 * with `:not()` guards standing in for the spread's own `!isSelected` /
 * `!isDisabled` conditions. The mode toggles had no hover state and get none
 * here.
 *
 * BORDER ORDERING mirrors the spread order the style objects had: the cell's
 * base `border: none` is overridden by the today ring only when the cell is not
 * selected (the selected spread never re-applied the ring), and the selected
 * background outranks the base but is disjoint from the hover rule by
 * construction. `border: none` is a color-free reset (exempt from the P-48
 * (0,4,0) floor); the mode toggle's and the today ring's real borders clear the
 * tenant's unlayered (0,3,1) `*` border-color floor at (0,5,0)+.
 *
 * `>` CHAINS THROUGHOUT: `data-part` is a shared vocabulary and `dateCellRender`
 * / `monthCellRender` inject arbitrary caller content inside the cells, so a
 * descendant selector could reach a nested component's own parts.
 *
 * Values transcribed verbatim from the `styles` object in `engines/rustic.tsx`.
 */

.rottay-calendar.rottay-calendar--rustic[data-part='root'] {
  background-color: var(--ds-calendar-bg, var(--ds-color-bg-elevated));
  border-radius: var(--ds-calendar-radius, 8px);
