/**
 * Modern Callout skin (WO-SKIN-05 checkpoint D2).
 *
 * DELIBERATELY UNLAYERED (P-47): every `rottay-*` layer sorts before Tailwind's
 * base layer, so a layered rule loses to preflight/DaisyUI regardless of
 * specificity. Unlayered outranks both and still yields to a caller's inline
 * `style`.
 *
 * SCOPE ROOT carries `rottay-callout-shell rottay-callout-shell--modern`
 * alongside the DaisyUI `.alert` class and `data-part='root'` + `data-tone`.
 * The dedicated `-shell` scope is mandatory: bare `.rottay-alert` /
 * `.rottay-alert-shell` are Alert's, and a rule anchored on a classname another
 * component renders repaints that component. `rottay-callout-shell` is
 * grep-verified free across CSS and CSS-in-JS.
 *
 * BORDER CHANNEL: Modern Callout declares no border inline, and DaisyUI's own
 * `.alert { border-width: var(--border) }` (which outranks preflight) is what
 * paints this root's border today. This skin therefore declares no border on the
 * root: a width here would be a border that does not exist today, and a lone
 * `border-color` longhand would leave DaisyUI's `var(--border)` in charge of the
 * width. The `border: none` on the close button is a color-free reset (exempt
 * from the P-48 (0,4,0) border floor).
