.rottay-callout-shell.rottay-callout-shell--modern[data-part='root'][data-tone='warning'] {
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ds-color-warning) 10%, transparent);
  color: var(--ds-color-warning);
}
.rottay-callout-shell.rottay-callout-shell--modern[data-part='root'][data-tone='error'] {
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ds-color-error) 10%, transparent);
  color: var(--ds-color-error);
}
.rottay-callout-shell.rottay-callout-shell--modern[data-part='root'][data-tone='success'] {
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ds-color-success) 10%, transparent);
  color: var(--ds-color-success);
}

/* ---- close button: ghost circle. Child combinator keeps the rule off any
        `data-part='close-button'` a caller's content may bring. ---- */
.rottay-callout-shell.rottay-callout-shell--modern[data-part='root'] > [data-part='close-button'] {
  background: transparent;
  color: var(--ds-color-text-primary);
  border-radius: 50%;
  border: none;
}

/**
 * Rustic Callout skin (WO-SKIN-05 checkpoint D2).
 *
 * DELIBERATELY UNLAYERED (P-47): a layered rule sorts before Tailwind's base
 * layer and loses to preflight; unlayered outranks preflight and still yields to
 * the caller's inline `style`.
 *
 * SCOPE ROOT carries `rottay-callout-shell rottay-callout-shell--rustic` +
 * `data-part='root'` + `data-tone` (alongside the untargeted legacy
 * `rottay-callout-rustic` / `rottay-callout--<variant>` names). The `-shell`
 * scope is mandatory: bare `.rottay-alert` / `.rottay-alert-shell` belong to
 * Alert, and a rule anchored on a classname another component renders repaints
 * that component. Rustic's root carries no DaisyUI `alert` class, so nothing
 * external composes onto its border channel.
 *
 * SPECIFICITY (P-48): the Platform-only Rottay artifact ships an unlayered
 * `html[data-tenant]:not([data-theme]):not(.light) *` at (0,3,1) that sets
 * border-color on every element. The left accent is a `border-left` SHORTHAND
 * (as it is inline) so width, style and color land atomically; it therefore
 * reaches (0,4,0) via the two shell classes + `[data-part='root']` +
