 * `color`/`thickness` are caller-overridable free-form props (`DividerProps`
 * accepts any CSS color string and either a preset or a raw px number), so
 * the resolved line value cannot be enumerated into a finite `data-*`
 * lookup the way a closed-enum channel can. It rides the `--ds-divider-line`
 * custom-property hatch instead -- set inline, every render, to the exact
 * string the removed `borderTop`/`borderLeft` keys used to hold (the same
 * hatch the migration kit sanctions for a runtime-computed value); the
 * fallback below matches `DEFAULT_COLORS.modern` + `THICKNESS_MAP.thin` +
 * the default `solid` variant so it is never actually reached in practice.
 * Text color's `plain` branch has the same shape: this engine stamps no
 * `data-plain` (rustic's own skin uses its existing `divider--plain` class
 * instead, since it already renders one), so `plain ? 'inherit' : token`
 * rides `--ds-divider-plain-color`.
 *
 * SPECIFICITY (P-48): every line rule paints a real border color on one axis
 * per orientation (the other axis is always the colorless reset `none`) and
 * must reach (0,4,0) -- the two root classes + `[data-part='root']` already
 * give (0,3,0), and `[data-orientation='...']` (with-text) or
 * `[data-with-text='false']` (plain) buys the 4th unit. Text color is
 * non-border and clears preflight unlayered at (0,3,0) or better. Values
 * transcribed verbatim from `engines/modern.tsx`.
 */

/* ---- line: with-text spans (was lineBeforeStyle/lineAfterStyle's
        borderTop/borderLeft, both driven by `isHorizontal`). ---- */
.rottay-divider.rottay-divider--modern[data-part='root'][data-orientation='horizontal'] [data-part='line-before'],
.rottay-divider.rottay-divider--modern[data-part='root'][data-orientation='horizontal'] [data-part='line-after'] {
  border-top: var(--ds-divider-line, 1px solid var(--ds-divider-color, oklch(0.746 0 0)));
  border-left: none;
}
.rottay-divider.rottay-divider--modern[data-part='root'][data-orientation='vertical'] [data-part='line-before'],
.rottay-divider.rottay-divider--modern[data-part='root'][data-orientation='vertical'] [data-part='line-after'] {
  border-left: var(--ds-divider-line, 1px solid var(--ds-divider-color, oklch(0.746 0 0)));
  border-top: none;
}

/* ---- line: plain divider, merged onto the root itself (was the simple-
        divider return path's `{ ...containerStyle, ...lineStyle }`). Gated
        to `data-with-text='false'` -- the with-text root never carries this
        channel (see header). ---- */
.rottay-divider.rottay-divider--modern[data-part='root'][data-orientation='horizontal'][data-with-text='false'] {
  border-top: var(--ds-divider-line, 1px solid var(--ds-divider-color, oklch(0.746 0 0)));
  border-left: none;
}
.rottay-divider.rottay-divider--modern[data-part='root'][data-orientation='vertical'][data-with-text='false'] {
  border-left: var(--ds-divider-line, 1px solid var(--ds-divider-color, oklch(0.746 0 0)));
  border-top: none;
}

/* ---- text: color (was textStyle.color's `plain` ternary). ---- */
.rottay-divider.rottay-divider--modern[data-part='root'] [data-part='text'] {
  color: var(--ds-divider-plain-color, var(--ds-color-text-secondary));
