 * resolved line value rides the `--ds-divider-line` custom-property hatch,
 * same as the modern skin. `borderRight`/`borderBottom` are always the
 * static literal `none` in the source (never conditional on anything caller-
 * supplied) -- transcribed here as plain, unconditional declarations, no
 * hatch needed. `plain`'s text-color branch DOES have a DOM signal on this
 * engine: `divider--plain` is already stamped by the component (only when
 * `plain && hasChildren`) -- keyed on directly, no hatch, no invented
 * anatomy.
 *
 * SPECIFICITY (P-48): every line rule paints a real border color on one axis
 * per orientation and must reach (0,4,0) -- the two root classes +
 * `[data-part='root']` already give (0,3,0), and `[data-orientation='...']`
 * (with-text) or `[data-with-text='false']` (plain) buys the 4th unit. Text
 * color is non-border and clears preflight unlayered at (0,3,0) or better.
 * Values transcribed verbatim from `engines/rustic.tsx`.
