/**
 * Rustic Image skin (WO-SKIN-05 checkpoint D1).
 *
 * DELIBERATELY UNLAYERED (P-47): no `rottay-*` layer can paint a component
 * (Tailwind's `@layer base` sorts after all of them). Unlayered outranks preflight
 * and still yields to the caller's inline `style`.
 *
 * SCOPE ROOT keeps `rottay-image-rustic` and adds `rottay-image rottay-image--rustic`
 * (fresh mints, grep-verified free) so the engine pair anchors every rule.
 *
 * The ZOOM DIALOG is not a descendant of the root: this engine returns a fragment
 * whose second child is the dialog, so no root-scoped selector can reach it. It gets
 * its own self-sufficient scope, `rottay-image-zoom rottay-image-zoom--rustic` —
 * the same standalone treatment WO-SKIN-02 gave the portaled picker panels. The
 * modern engine has no zoom dialog at all; that asymmetry is preserved.
 *
 * `--ds-image-resolved-radius` carries `RADIUS_MAP[radius]`, one value the object
 * applied to five different elements. The `radius` prop is not stamped as an
 * attribute, and the value is a single inherited custom property here — set once on
 * the root, read by every part below. It is deliberately NOT the public
 * `--ds-image-radius` token (which the classic engine's theme already consumes);
 * overloading that name would leak a per-instance value into a shared token.
 *
 * SPECIFICITY (P-48): rules carrying a border COLOUR must clear the tenant's
 * unlayered `*` floor at (0,3,1); the repeated `[data-part]` takes them past
 * (0,4,0). The unbordered `border: none` and the close button's are colour-free
 * resets and are exempt. Both frames stay SHORTHANDS because preflight zeroes
 * `border-width` on every element.
 *
 * KEYFRAME: the per-mount `<style>` injecting `rusticImagePulse` is replaced by an
