/**
 * Rustic List skin (WO-SKIN-05 checkpoint D2). Covers the two exports of
 * `engines/rustic.tsx` that paint -- List and Meta. Rustic's `Item` carries no
 * paint at all (pure layout), so it gets no scope class and no rules: the
 * modern/rustic asymmetry is transcribed, not levelled.
 *
 * DELIBERATELY UNLAYERED (P-47): a layered rule sorts before Tailwind's base
 * layer and loses to preflight; unlayered outranks preflight and still yields to
 * the caller's inline `style`.
 *
 * SCOPES: `rottay-list rottay-list--rustic` + `data-part='root'` +
 * `data-bordered` + `data-loading`; `rottay-list-item-meta
 * rottay-list-item-meta--rustic`. Meta is usable standalone, so it carries its
 * own scope rather than hanging off the List root's. All grep-verified free.
 *
 * THE BORDERLESS BRANCH HAS NO RULES, DELIBERATELY. Every border here was
 * `bordered ? '<value>' : undefined`, and an `undefined` key is one ReactDOM
 * never writes -- so the borderless list falls to preflight's `border-width: 0`
 * and an initial `border-radius: 0`, which is exactly what an absent rule gives.
 *
 * Inside `[data-loading='true']` the tree is a pure skeleton with no caller
 * content, so those rules may safely use descendant selectors (their targets sit
 * under unclassed layout divs). Everywhere else uses child combinators, since
 * `data-part` is a shared vocabulary and List renders caller content.
 *
 * SPECIFICITY (P-48): border-bearing rules clear the tenant's unlayered (0,3,1)
 * `*` border-color floor at (0,4,0)+. Values transcribed verbatim from
 * `engines/rustic.tsx`.
 */

/* ============================ List (container) ============================ */

.rottay-list.rottay-list--rustic[data-part='root'][data-bordered='true'] {
  border: 1px solid var(--ds-list-border-color, var(--ds-color-border));
