 * free), never a bare `[data-part='bubble']` -- `data-part` is a shared
 * vocabulary, and a bare part selector would claim every bubble in the fleet.
 * The wrapper root keeps NO scope class: it paints nothing, and `rottay-tooltip`
 * is a live personality/tenant hook (entrance animation, z-index) that modern's
 * wrapper does not carry today.
 *
 * `top`/`left` STAY INLINE: they come from `getBoundingClientRect()` on every
 * frame the tooltip is positioned -- genuine runtime data, and not paint.
 *
 * SPECIFICITY (P-48): the Platform-only Rottay artifact ships an unlayered
 * `html[data-tenant]:not([data-theme]):not(.light) *` at (0,3,1) that sets
