/**
 * Modern CommandPalette skin (WO-SKIN-06 CK-G).
 *
 * DELIBERATELY UNLAYERED (P-47): every `rottay-*` layer sorts before Tailwind's
 * `base` layer, so a layered rule loses to preflight regardless of specificity.
 * Unlayered outranks preflight + DaisyUI and still yields to a caller's inline
 * `style` (the root/dialog forward the caller's `style`/`className`).
 *
 * SCOPE ROOT: the palette's outer `<div>` carries
 * `ds-pattern-command-palette ds-engine-modern` + `data-part='root'`; every painted
 * element is a descendant with its own `data-part`. NOT portaled — the dialog is a
 * `position:fixed` DOM descendant of the tenant-scoped root, so descendant selectors
 * from the scope class reach it (no portal-root escape).
 *
 * SPECIFICITY (P-48): the Platform-only Rottay artifact ships an unlayered
 * `html[data-tenant]:not([data-theme]):not(.light) *` at (0,3,1) setting
 * `border-color` on every element. A rule that paints a border COLOR must reach
 * (0,4,0): two root classes (0,2,0) + the target's `data-part` REPEATED (0,2,0).
 * Non-border paint wins unlayered at (0,3,0). A `border: none` reset carries no color
 * and is exempt.
 *
 * TOKENS: modern reads GENERIC tokens (--ds-color, --ds-surface, --ds-elevation)
 * and never the --ds-command-palette-* namespace — that namespace is rustic-only, and
 * mapping modern onto it would newly make modern tenant-themeable through a channel it
 * has never honored. Two vocabularies, one per engine; the split is preserved verbatim.
 *
 * INTERACTION: the keyboard-active row keys on `[data-active='true']`; pointer hover
 * keys on `:hover:not([data-active='true'])` so it never repaints the keyboard-selected
 * row — the exact `activeIndex !== idx` guard the removed onMouseEnter/Leave writes had.
 *
 * Values transcribed verbatim from `engines/modern.tsx`.
 */

