/**
 * Modern NotificationCenter skin (WO-SKIN-06 CK-F unit F1).
 *
 * DELIBERATELY UNLAYERED (P-76): every `rottay-*` layer sorts before Tailwind's
 * `base` layer, so a layered rule cannot paint these elements at all.
 *
 * SCOPE ROOT: the root `<div>` carries `ds-pattern-notification-center
 * ds-engine-modern` + `data-part='root'`; every painted element is a descendant
 * with its own `data-part`.
 *
 * SPECIFICITY (P-48): the Platform-only Rottay artifact ships an unlayered
 * `html[data-tenant]:not([data-theme]):not(.light) *` at (0,3,1) setting
 * `border-color` on every element. A rule that paints a border COLOR must reach
 * (0,4,0): two root classes (0,2,0) + the target's `data-part` REPEATED (0,2,0).
 * Non-border paint (background, color, border-radius, box-shadow) wins unlayered
 * at (0,3,0).
 *
 * DEAD CODE: `typeBgStyles` (icon-container tint) in modern.tsx is defined but
 * never referenced in JSX -- the orchestrator's pre-step audit confirmed this at
 * runtime. There is no icon-container tint rule here because there is no DOM
 * element to anchor one to; the dead const is left in place in the TSX per the
 * CK-F contract addendum. Only `typeColorStyles` (the glyph color, live) moved.
 *
 * TOKENS: modern's "info" type resolves to `--ds-color-info`; rustic's resolves
 * to `--ds-color-primary` -- a genuine cross-engine disagreement, not just a
 * mechanism difference. modern's unread-row tint is an ad hoc `color-mix`;
 * rustic's is the named `--ds-color-primary-50` scale token. Both preserved
 * verbatim, not unified (WO-SKIN-06 CK-F contract §0).
 *
 * INTERACTION: the dismiss button's hover brighten was imperative
 * (`.style.opacity =` in onMouseEnter/onMouseLeave, uncounted paint). The rule
 * below replaces it; opacity's static 0.3 rest value stays inline on the element
 * since opacity itself is not a paint channel this program moves.
 *
 * Values transcribed verbatim from `engines/modern.tsx`.
 */

